--- body ---
## Context

Child of tracker 0613 (goal 1 of the ladder), gap B. `Ticket-ref: tickets/0613`
— this ticket does not close the tracker; gap C remains blocked elsewhere.

`R15-uninstall-removes-declared-state` is `not-offered` for zoteus. The
2026-09-03 ruling (0613's log) retired the earlier reading that zoteus must
grow a callable uninstall verb: an external MCP server has no host uninstall
lifecycle to hook, so the ratified surface for this architecture class is a
**published removal procedure** the harness can execute verbatim and sweep.
Two preconditions the ruling attached: TMPDIR/XDG redirection in the arena
(status not re-checked here — 0613's log said only HOME was redirected as of
2026-09-03), and a dedicated account owning the arena rather than the
operator's home — **that second precondition is done**: ticket 0625 closed.

Form is already decided (0613's log, 2026-09-03T13:43Z): not an upstream
issue asking the maintainer to write this — **we draft it ourselves**, in
this project's own documentation voice (`docs/configuration.md`,
`docs/semantic-search.md`), using the declared derived-state roots from
`bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py`'s Declaration (data dir, model cache
under it since upstream PR #27) phrased as steps a user follows, with the
pre-PR-#27 case as the worked example of why "just delete the data
directory" was wrong before that merge.

**Per this repo's own upstream discipline**: a repo-side PR is the spec/
measurement record, not the shipped artifact — the actual upstream
submission is a separate, GOVERNANCE.md-gated action, not something this
ticket files on its own. This ticket's deliverable is the drafted procedure,
committed in this repo, ready for that later hand-off.

## Actions

1. Read `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py`'s `Declaration`
   (`derived_state_roots=(self.data_dir,)`, ~line 280): **exactly one**
   declared root, `self.arena / "data"`, which maps onto `ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` in
   `_env()` (~line 314). That is arena-relative — a test fixture path, not
   what a user sees. The real default is `defaultDataDir()` in the fork
   checkout's `src/lib/paths.ts`: `$ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` if set, else
   `~/Library/Application Support/zoteus` (macOS), `%APPDATA%\zoteus`
   (Windows), or `${XDG_DATA_HOME:-~/.local/share}/zoteus` (everything
   else). The draft's removal step names *this* pair (env var / OS default),
   never the arena path. The model cache has no separate declared root — it
   is `<ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR>/models`, a subdirectory of the one root, per PR #27.
2. Draft the content in `verification/UNINSTALL-DRAFT-0630.md` — this repo's
   existing convention for a staged-but-unsent upstream artifact (see
   `verification/ISSUE-DRAFT-0530.md`, `verification/UPSTREAM-PR-POOLING-0612.md`):
   a short preamble (revision measured against, ruling citations, explicit
   "not sent — GOVERNANCE.md lane" note) followed by the literal content
   meant for the upstream file. That upstream file is `UNINSTALL.md` at the
   fork's **repo root**, not under `docs/` — matching `fork/CHANGELOG.md`,
   `fork/CONTRIBUTING.md`, `fork/PRIVACY.md`, which sit at root while topic
   guides (`configuration.md`, `semantic-search.md`, …) sit under `fork/docs/`.
   All of these paths are **inside the `fork/` checkout, not this repo** —
   they don't exist until `make upstream-checkout` + `npm ci && npm run build`
   has run (same recipe 0629 already documents; `fork/` is gitignored here and
   absent on a fresh checkout). `fork/docs/configuration.md` and
   `fork/docs/semantic-search.md` are cited for *voice and structure* (bold
   lead sentences, concrete paths in backticks, e.g. `semantic-search.md`'s
   "Where the files are" — "removing the data directory removes everything
   the index ever wrote"), not as the destination directory.
3. Include the pre-PR-#27 case as the worked example, sourced from the fork
   checkout's commit `5ae398a` / `998865e`
   (`fix(search): cache on-device model weights under the data directory`,
   merged 2026-08-29): before it, `@huggingface/transformers`' default
   `env.cacheDir` held the downloaded weights inside the package's own
   install — and, for a bundled desktop install pointed at a global module
   via `ZOTEUS_TRANSFORMERS_PATH`, in a global `node_modules` that outlives
   even an extension uninstall — so "delete the data directory" alone left
   the single largest artifact (~25 MB today, gigabytes for larger models)
   behind. After the merge, `LocalEmbeddingProvider` pins `env.cacheDir` to
   `<ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR>/models` before the pipeline is constructed.
4. Record the TMPDIR/XDG finding precisely — **re-measured for this ticket,
   and it is sharper than 0613's log's "only HOME, in one adapter"**: as of
   this pass, `bench/acceptance/adapters/zoteus.py`'s `_env()` (lines
   311-324) redirects only a handful of `ZOTEUS_*` variables, merged onto
   the *full* operator environment
   (`self._posture.wrap(cmd, {**os.environ, **env})`, line 372) — it
   redirects nothing else, not even `HOME`. Four *other* adapters
   (`beaver.py`, `zotero_core_6012.py`, `zotero_mcp.py`, `zotseek.py`)
   redirect `HOME`; `zoteus.py` — the one this ticket's rung is about —
   does not. `TMPDIR` is redirected nowhere in `bench/acceptance/`. `XDG_`
   appears exactly once, `XDG_CACHE_HOME` in `zotero_mcp.py` only, blanked
   so it falls under that adapter's redirected `HOME`. `sandbox.py` has no
   `TMPDIR`/`XDG_`/`HOME` handling at all. Log this in this ticket's own
   log as an open precondition gap — it does not block drafting the doc
   (the doc's correctness is independent of it), but R15 cannot be graded
   green for zoteus until it closes.
5. Do NOT open an upstream PR from this ticket. Commit the draft in this
   repo and reference the GOVERNANCE.md lane that owns the hand-off (`## The
   bounds`, contained-PR form — a docs change of the shape that merged
   verbatim twice, #27 and #28).

## Test

- New file `tests/test_uninstall_doc.py` (offline, no process spawned — same
  shape as `tests/test_acceptance_adapter_zoteus.py`'s construction-only
  tests): builds a `Zoteus` adapter instance to read
  `.declaration.derived_state_roots`, reads
  `verification/UNINSTALL-DRAFT-0630.md`, and asserts a **symbolic**
  correspondence, not a literal-path string match:
  - exactly one root is declared (`len(derived_state_roots) == 1`);
  - the draft's removal step names the symbol `ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` (env var /
    OS-default pair) as the thing to delete — never the harness's own
    arena-relative path, which would make the test fixture leak into the
    published doc;
  - the draft states the model cache lives *under* that same root (a
    substring match for `models` tied to the same step, not a second listed
    location) — this is the exact clause PR #27 made true and a future
    regression could make false again silently.
  A literal-string match (asserting the resolved arena path like
  `Path(tmp)/data` appears in the prose) would be tautological: that path is
  a test fixture, never seen by a real user, so it can only catch a typo in
  the test file itself, not drift in what the target actually declares or
  writes. The check must go through the symbol both sides share
  (`ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR`), matched structurally, not counted.
- Positive control before trusting it: run the new test against a
  deliberately wrong draft first (e.g. one naming a second, invented root,
  or omitting the model-cache-is-under-the-root sentence) and confirm it
  fails red, per this repo's own red-first-check discipline (the "all-clear
  indistinguishable from 'I could not look'" principle applied throughout
  this repo's verification notes and DECISIONS.md, e.g. R20's surrogate
  revalidation entry).

## Verification

- [x] `verification/UNINSTALL-DRAFT-0630.md` drafted, in
      `docs/configuration.md`/`docs/semantic-search.md`'s voice, its one
      removal step naming `ZOTEUS_DATA_DIR` (env var / OS default from
      `paths.ts`'s `defaultDataDir()`), never the harness's arena path
- [x] Pre-#27 worked example included, sourced from fork commit `5ae398a` /
      `998865e`
- [x] `tests/test_uninstall_doc.py` exists, is offline, and was seen failing
      red against a deliberately wrong draft (positive control) before being
      trusted green
- [x] TMPDIR/XDG redirection status recorded in this ticket's log: confirmed
      incomplete, with the precise finding above (zoteus.py redirects
      nothing but `ZOTEUS_*` vars, not even `HOME`; `TMPDIR` is redirected
      nowhere in `bench/acceptance/`; only `zotero_mcp.py` touches
      `XDG_CACHE_HOME`)
- [x] No upstream PR opened by this ticket (true of this ticket's own PR
      #332; the actual filing happened as a later, separate action — see log)

## Invariants

- The dedicated-account precondition (0625) is not touched or re-verified
  here — it's independently closed.
- Gap C stays out of scope; this ticket does not touch R22.

## Exit criteria

- The removal procedure is drafted, committed, and traceable to the
  adapter's Declaration (met — placement moved from a standalone
  `UNINSTALL.md` to a `README.md` section plus `docs/uninstall.md`, see log),
  and 0613's log records the draft plus the TMPDIR/XDG redirection finding.
  Sending it upstream is `GOVERNANCE.md`'s lane, not this ticket's scope —
  done as a separate action, recorded below.
